  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 251 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nBy Friday, the weak cold front and its associated disturbance exit \nto the southeast, with rain chances diminishing and southerly low \nlevel winds advecting warmer temperatures. On Saturday, most \nlocations will see temperatures in excess of 100 degrees, \napproaching record temperatures. As the weekend progresses, an upper \nlevel ridge is expected to emerge to the east, advecting in cooler \ngulf moisture, bringing temperatures gradually down to the mid to \nupper 90s through early next week. Additionally, the moisture \nadvection into the area may be enough to bring some scattered \nshowers and storms in the higher elevations and the surrounding \nplains west of the Pecos River.",
